## Step 2 — upload assets (strongest signal first)

Claude Design extracts four categories: 色彩調色板 / 排版 / 元件 / 版面配置模式.
Uploading real-example pages first yields the strongest brand signal.

- [ ] Upload `assets/sample-landing.html`
- [ ] Upload `assets/sample-dashboard.html`
- [ ] Upload `design.md`
- [ ] Upload `design.tokens.yaml`
{{#HAS_LOGO}}
- [ ] Upload `{{LOGO_PATH}}`
{{/HAS_LOGO}}
{{#HAS_PALETTE_IMAGE}}
- [ ] Upload `{{PALETTE_IMAGE_PATH}}`
{{/HAS_PALETTE_IMAGE}}
{{#HAS_TYPE_SPECIMEN}}
- [ ] Upload `{{TYPE_SPECIMEN_PATH}}`
{{/HAS_TYPE_SPECIMEN}}
{{#HAS_TENANT_OVERLAY}}
- [ ] Upload `tenant-overlay.example.yaml` (reference only; Claude Design does not ingest multi-tenant natively)
{{/HAS_TENANT_OVERLAY}}

## Step 3 — validate

Create a test project inside Claude Design and run the three brand-specific
prompts:

- [ ] `{{TEST_PROMPT_1}}`
- [ ] `{{TEST_PROMPT_2}}`
- [ ] `{{TEST_PROMPT_3}}`

For each output, check the five failure signals (see
`references/claude-design-upload.md § failure-signals`):

- [ ] Palette does not drift toward generic SaaS defaults
- [ ] Typography loads the correct family (not fallback)
- [ ] Components feel consistent with sample pages
- [ ] Dark mode renders correctly
- [ ] Per-page layouts respect brand intent (may require manual engineering
      per § post-upload-manual-actions)

If any check fails, iterate: add additional assets (more sample pages,
additional screenshots) and re-generate. Do not publish until validation
passes.

## Step 4 — publish

- [ ] Toggle 已發佈 / Published to ON
- [ ] Verify at Claude Design homepage → new projects default to this
      system (not Claude Platform Design System)
- [ ] Notify team that **{{BRAND_NAME}} v{{VERSION}}** is live

